      "text_raw": "In practice, the current\nratio is not that accurate.\nIndeed, both transistor may\nnot operate at the same v\nDS\nvoltage. A difference in v\nDS\nwill give a difference in cur-\nrent, as the i −v charac-\nDS DS\nteristic is not that flat.\nThis difference is easily\ncalculated. It is related to\nthe Early voltage and hence\nto the channel length L .\n2\nThe larger the channel\nlength, the flatter the curve\nand the smaller the current\ndifference will be.\nIt is difficult to make that\nv voltage difference zero. This is why we resort to circuit techniques.\nDS",
